NODE id=github.com/paxlabs-inc/chronos/internal/store.Store.ClaimDue kind=method
  digest=b3:4bb47e9c07f35927ed11e7ad1f74967017098563e17207773fe3a2cf7396ca2e file=chronos/internal/store/alarms.go range=129:164 lang=go exported=true byte_range=4478:5709
  sig=func (s *Store) ClaimDue(ctx context.Context, batch int, lease time.Duration) ([]types.Alarm, error)
  doc=ClaimDue atomically leases up to `batch` active alarms whose next_fire_at has\npassed and that are not currently leased (claimed_at older than `lease`).\nFOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED so concurrent/future workers never double-claim\n(dispatch.claim). A crash mid-fire leaves the lease, which expires after\n`lease` and is reclaimed — at-least-once delivery (invariant i3).
EDGES
  ^contains=github.com/paxlabs-inc/chronos/internal/store.Store
  ^defines=github.com/paxlabs-inc/chronos/internal/store/alarms.go

